611
00:26:41.240 --> 00:26:42.920
I think I'm Loggins and Messina.

612
00:26:42.920 --> 00:26:43.640
I am, too.

613
00:26:43.920 --> 00:26:45.180
And I didn't even know it.

614
00:26:45.260 --> 00:26:47.860
I didn't even know it was.

615
00:26:47.940 --> 00:26:49.320
It just cracked me up.

616
00:26:49.440 --> 00:26:54.600
Like, I don't know which writer in the writer's room pitched this very small, subtle joke that

617
00:26:54.600 --> 00:27:00.140
Stanley would not like Messina and only want solo Loggins, but it really cracked me up.

618
00:27:00.240 --> 00:27:03.300
You guys, I'm a total dork for little, tiny jokes like that.

619
00:27:03.300 --> 00:27:08.980
Well, I noticed something about this scene, which is that it was very windy outside.

620
00:27:09.300 --> 00:27:10.520
Did you see the wind?

621
00:27:10.920 --> 00:27:11.100
No.

622
00:27:11.100 --> 00:27:11.780
So windy.

623
00:27:12.120 --> 00:27:16.300
No, I think I was so fixated on that couplet of dialogue.

624
00:27:16.600 --> 00:27:21.840
Well, I noticed it because that's kind of unusual for LA, but I thought it really sold it as Florida.

625
00:27:22.240 --> 00:27:22.820
Oh, yeah.

626
00:27:23.140 --> 00:27:24.260
Made it look very tropical.

627
00:27:24.260 --> 00:27:24.840
Yeah.

628
00:27:25.420 --> 00:27:29.880
Well, these guys are all going to head to their meeting, and in the meantime, we're going to head to Scranton.

629
00:27:30.620 --> 00:27:34.400
Andy's going to walk out of his office and notice how incredibly quiet it is.

630
00:27:34.600 --> 00:27:35.780
Yeah, Creed likes it.

631
00:27:35.840 --> 00:27:37.520
He's already written 12 plays.

632
00:27:37.720 --> 00:27:37.940
Yeah.

633
00:27:38.600 --> 00:27:44.180
Can we please, please have an episode somewhere where we just watch one of Creed's plays?

634
00:27:44.200 --> 00:27:45.500
Why didn't that exist?

635
00:27:46.080 --> 00:27:48.620
Because it would be utter nonsense.

636
00:27:48.980 --> 00:27:49.460
I know.

637
00:27:49.800 --> 00:27:51.400
It would make no sense.

638
00:27:52.240 --> 00:27:54.840
Pam wonders, wait, why is it so quiet?

639
00:27:54.840 --> 00:27:59.460
She realizes that it's because no one took the phone off voicemail.

640
00:27:59.840 --> 00:28:00.140
